## Test Plan & Strategy

There is a `test_inputs.sh` file that has a shell script in it that we'll use to test this.
There is also a `test_mysh.c` file that is actually there to run the tests.

To test the interactive mode, there is a `posix_openpt()` to open a pseudo-terminal.
So it tests the interactive mode there.
Seems to work.

The testing suite checks for redirections, pipelines, wildcards, syntax errors and such.

## Note about NixOS

Some stuff here is adjusted to run on NixOS.
I'm not sure how well it'll run on the school computers.

I tested this in a Docker container running Debian.
Seems to work there too.

This is the Dockerfile:

```Dockerfile
FROM debian:bookworm-slim

RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
    build-essential \
    gcc \
    make \
    gdb \
    valgrind \
    clang \
    strace \
    debianutils \
    coreutils \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

WORKDIR /workspace

CMD ["/bin/bash"]
```

I don't know how to spin up the actual school computers and I'm too lazy to figure it out right now.
Just wanna go to bed already I have a midterm.
We're just gonna run with this.
Life is too short ya'll.
